-- Since top-level initialisation rule I2, `medaka check`, `run` and `build` refuse this
-- program with T-TOPLEVEL-EFFECT before any engine runs: `side` is a top-level value
-- whose initialiser performs <Stdout>, and a value is initialised once at startup with
-- an empty effect row (test/rejection_parity_fixtures.txt pins that on native and wasm).
-- The prelude-free llvm probe runs no typechecker, so it still emits the program with
-- its old lazy meaning (`side` never forced, prints "ok") and keeps that golden.
main = if False then side else putStrLn "ok"

side = putStrLn "BOOM"
